The memory safety scan in src/memory_safety.rs is adapted from NousResearch/hermes-agent tools/threat_patterns.py at commit 36b98bcced7f3c22d08dd1119240e726b3928e3d. Its upstream MIT license and copyright are included in that source and LICENSE.hermes.

Orialis protocol behavior and original baseline are grounded in J-X-C-Z/Orialis at f9a064bf05b18265afd26905e7240777d4ce355c. The bundled experiment is not an official upstream release and is not a complete Hermes replacement.

The native file patch implementation in src/file_patch.rs and src/file_patch/fuzzy.rs and src/file_patch/v4a.rs, together with its source-derived contract fixtures, is adapted from NousResearch/hermes-agent tools/fuzzy_match.py, tools/escape_drift_autocorrect.py, tools/patch_parser.py, and tools/file_operations_common.py at commit 36b98bcced7f3c22d08dd1119240e726b3928e3d. Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research. The upstream MIT copyright and permission notice are retained in LICENSE.hermes. Changes include translation to Rust, pure planning APIs, deterministic resource bounds, root-relative path restrictions, and integration with the native approval and stale-state checks.

The matching-block implementation in src/file_patch/sequence.rs is a Rust adaptation of CPython difflib.SequenceMatcher, not a clean-room independent implementation. Its longest-match scan, autojunk filtering, work queue, earliest-match tie behavior, adjacent-block merge, and ratio calculation were ported from the locally installed Python 3.12.14 difflib.py. CPython's applicable license and copyright notices are retained in LICENSE.python, copied unchanged from that installation's lib/python3.12/LICENSE.txt. This file contains the Python Software Foundation License Version 2 and the retained historical Python license notices.

Summary of changes to the adapted CPython code: translated the SequenceMatcher matching-block and ratio subset to Rust; replaced Python containers with Rust containers; added a deterministic comparison-work budget and typed limit errors; used Unicode character sequences with separate UTF-8 span mapping in the caller; omitted user-supplied junk callbacks, mutable matcher caching, and unrelated difflib APIs. The Python Software Foundation and other upstream authors do not endorse this experiment.
